  "reason": "A snapshot that merely parses is not trustworthy. The reference states that only unmodified snapshots from a trusted, compatible producer may be restored, and that the caller must establish provenance and integrity before loading — Monty does not authenticate snapshots or fully validate their contents. Invalid snapshots have no correctness or availability guarantees, and a snapshot is only ever taken between turns, so max_turn_duration_secs has nothing to carry. A timeout alone never proves that no effect occurred, and neither restored memory nor a timeout establishes that no external effect happened. Therefore parsing alone is insufficient; provenance and integrity must be verified before restoring bytes received through an untrusted channel.",
